Preheat oven to 400°F (prep and assembly will take around ~{45%minutes} minutes with store-bought polenta).

== Make Filling ==

Heat @olive oil{2%tbsp} in a #large skillet{} over medium-high heat. Sauté @onion{1}(diced), stirring until tender, about ~{5%minutes}. Add @garlic{4-6%cloves}(roughly chopped) and cook ~{2%minutes} more. 

Turn the skillet to medium (or medium-low) and add @mushrooms{12-16%ounces}(sliced), @salt{1/2%tsp}, @pepper{1/2%tsp}, and @Italian seasoning{1%tsp}, and sauté until the mushrooms release their liquid and it evaporates, about ~{10%minutes}. Add @baby spinach{2 heaping handfuls}(chopped) and wilt, mixing to combine, adding a splash of water if needed. Cook off any liquid and adjust @salt{} to your taste.

== Make Red Pepper Sauce ==

Add the drained @diced tomatoes{14%ounces can} to the blender and add @roasted red pepper{1/2 - 3/4%cup}. Add @olive oil{2%tbsp}, @salt{1/2%tsp}, @pepper{1/2%tsp}, @smoked paprika{1%tsp}, @cumin{1%tsp}, @sugar{1%tsp} and @Italian seasoning{1%tsp}. Blend until creamy and smooth. If the sauce is too thick to get the motor running, add a little water (a tablespoon at a time) just to get it going. Taste; it should have a sweet smoky flavor.

== Prepare Polento ==

It’s easiest to cut the @polenta{2 x 18-ounce tubes} in half, then in quarters, so each quarter yields 3 equal slices. This gives 12 slices from each tube, about 3/4 inch thick.

== Assemble ==

Spray a #9×13-inch baking dish{} with @olive oil{}. Place @sauce{1/2%cup} on the bottom, coating it evenly. Add the first layer of polenta (there are 2 layers). Top with all the filling, spreading it out evenly. Dot with spoonfuls of @ricotta cheese{6%ounces}(or vegan tofu ricotta). Sprinkle lightly with @salt{}, @pepper{}, and @nutmeg{generous pinch}. Top with @mozzarella cheese{1-2 cups}(grated). Pour @sauce{1/2%cup} lightly over the cheese. Then, top with a final layer of polenta. Pour some sauce over the top (you may not need all of it), and use a spatula to coat the polenta evenly. Save the remaining sauce for touching up after you remove the foil. You could do this all ahead and refrigerate for ~{24%hours}.

At this point, you could add more cheese on top or keep it a little leaner — up to you. Cover tightly with parchment and foil and bake ~{20%minutes}. Remove parchment/foil and bake uncovered for ~{15-20%minutes} until bubbling and warmed through. If you want it “saucy,” add more sauce.

When the polenta lasagna is finished cooking, you could drizzle it lightly with the pesto or serve it on the side.

== Optional: Make Pesto Drizzle ==

While it’s baking, make the pesto drizzle. To make the pesto drizzle, simply place @basil{1 cup}(packed), @olive oil{1/2%cup}, @garlic{1%clove}(fat), @salt{}, and @pepper{} to taste in a food processor and pulse until combined.